2. Product truth and boundaries

2.1 Aetheris Technology

Positioning: a business research and diagnostics company studying how people, decisions, processes and systems interact inside organizations. Its Golden Report / X-Ray approach is intended to connect externally observable signals, internal workflow evidence where authorized, and prioritized hypotheses into a coherent account of where value may be slipping away. The wider system includes research outputs, company-oriented intelligence, evidence views and report-driven workspaces. A diagnostic is not a certified audit and must not assert monetary losses without defensible inputs.

Core jobs to be done: map the end-to-end revenue or delivery process; identify broken handoffs; separate symptoms from root-cause hypotheses; quantify exposure only where data permit; assign owners, decisions and measurements; decide which workflow or integration to change first.

2.2 Mindprint Software by Aetheris

Mindprint uses public and user-provided professional material to organize evidence-linked observations across communication, thinking, decisions, trust, priorities and leadership. The product has Quick, Full and Intel report views, interactive mind maps, a 3D connection brain and person/company comparison concepts. The consumer storefront has been configured for a free preview, a $49 Full report and a $99 Intel edition; production payment readiness and market acceptance require independent verification.

The meaningful commercial promise is evidence organization and more useful questions. Individual behavior forecasts should be conditional, grounded and explicitly uncertain. It should never promise access to a person’s private thoughts, make medical or disability inferences, or be used as the sole basis of hiring, promotion, firing, lending or another high-stakes decision.

