7. Mindprint: personas, purchase occasions and packaging

7.1 The founder preparing for a high-stakes conversation

Persona: owner of a $3M–$30M business. A strategic partnership, difficult client, new executive or critical vendor discussion is imminent. Success means showing up with sharper questions and fewer unfounded assumptions. Will pay if the source quality is visible, report is immediately useful, and the analysis takes less time than manual research. Likely channel: LinkedIn professional content, referred advisers, decision-making communities.

7.2 The repeat-user adviser

Persona: fractional COO, executive coach, operating partner, leadership consultant or sophisticated agency owner with recurring executive conversations. This is arguably the higher lifetime-value buyer than a one-time curious consumer. Success means repeatable and ethically credible preparation, exportable briefings, consistency across clients, and permission controls. Commercial test: report credits or a constrained team package rather than unlimited use before usage costs are known.

7.3 Organizational sponsor

Persona: managing partner or COO responsible for a team whose communication delays decisions. The buyer does not want an abstract “personality score.” They want a facilitated map that links participant statements, roles and observed process failures to questions and specific changes in meetings, decisions or ownership. Require consent and a written boundary between research signals and performance evaluation.

